title: 'cpanfile: Rex::LibSSH must be recommends, not requires'
updated: 2026-09-24T19:49:33Z
---

cpanfile currently has:

requires 'Rex::LibSSH', '0.004';

This was deliberately changed from `recommends` to `requires` in commit a708642 ("Require Rex::LibSSH 0.004 host-key check, fix cpanfile deps"), but nothing under lib/ actually `use`s or `require`s Rex::LibSSH (checked: no hard use/require anywhere in lib/). It is invoked only indirectly, by the operators Rexfile via `set connection => "LibSSH"`, per the documented SFTP-less path (_check_connection in Rex::Rancher.pm dies with an actionable message pointing at Rex::LibSSH only when no SFTP subsystem is available and LibSSH was not selected).

Making it a hard `requires` breaks installability for anyone deploying to a host that *does* have a working SFTP subsystem (the majority path outside Hetzner dedicated) - they would be forced to pull in Rex::LibSSH (and its Net::LibSSH/libssh C dependency) for no reason.

Fix: change back to `recommends 'Rex::LibSSH', '0.004';` in cpanfile. Keep the 0.004 pin (matches the latest released CPAN version, GETTY/Rex-LibSSH-0.004.tar.gz - correct as-is).

Found during pre-release audit at 0b97665. Assign to rex-rancher-worker.
